# ==============================================================================
# Files excluded from the public repository.
#
# Grouped by reason rather than alphabetically, because the first two groups
# are the ones that would actually hurt if they leaked and they deserve to be
# read, not skimmed.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Member data — never commit, under any circumstances
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# challenge.db holds real names, email addresses and password hashes for a live
# search-and-rescue team. uploads/ holds their photos and their recorded GPX
# tracks, which are movement data tied to identifiable people. Neither is
# needed to run the app: tools/init_db.py builds an empty schema and
# app/__init__.py creates the upload subdirectories at startup.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.bak
app/uploads/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real configuration lives in /etc/challenge.env on the server, root-owned and
# mode 600, loaded by systemd via EnvironmentFile. Nothing that resembles a
# credential belongs in this tree. challenge.env.example documents the
# variables the app expects, with placeholder values only.
*.env
.env
challenge.env
!challenge.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python build artifacts
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local working files — useful to the maintainer, noise to everyone else
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md and the commenting guide describe how this project is worked on
# rather than what it does, and the deploy notes and route files are specific
# to one team's operations. They stay on disk; they just don't ship.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
DEPLOY-NOTES.md
educational_commenting_guide.md
To Test/
*.zip
*.gpx
challenge-announcement-*.txt
flag-slabbath-notes.txt
